# tests/eval-then, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. `eval-path-then` exists ONLY inside a worker — it is the way
# out for a job that must have an expression walked but may not block on a run
# — so the thing under test is reached natively here. The client was only a way
# to obtain a reference `eval-path` to compare against, and that comparison was
# a claim about client/server parity rather than about this verb.
#
# What replaces it is sharper and needs no client: evaluating a `run`-valued
# expression must produce exactly what RUNNING that request produces. The test
# forms the same request itself with `prepare-request` and compares result
# hashes, so the assertion is about evaluation, not about who asked for it.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --build:@=build.sh
